WEBVTT

1
00:01:14.992 --> 00:01:19.872
<i>Once, when I was six years old. I read
a book about the primeval forest.</i>

2
00:01:22.708 --> 00:01:24.042
<i>The book said:</i>

3
00:01:24.168 --> 00:01:27.796
<i>"All of constrictors swallow their
prey whole, without chewing it."</i>

4
00:01:32.176 --> 00:01:37.014
<i>I pondered this deeply. And
then, I did my first drawing.</i>

5
00:01:38.182 --> 00:01:40.559
<i>I showed my masterpiece
to grown-ups.</i>

6
00:01:40.684 --> 00:01:43.103
<i>And, asked if the drawing
frightened them.</i>

7
00:01:43.187 --> 00:01:44.271
<i>Frightened?</i>

8
00:01:44.354 --> 00:01:47.149
<i>Why should anyone
be frightened of a hat?</i>

9
00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:48.817
<i>Grown-ups!</i>

10
00:01:48.984 --> 00:01:51.320
<i>They never understand
anything by themselves.</i>

11
00:01:52.029 --> 00:01:54.823
<i>So, I made another drawing.</i>

12
00:01:55.908 --> 00:01:58.619
<i>Here is! My advice is
stick to arithmetic.</i>

13
00:01:58.702 --> 00:02:00.996
<i>- History.
- And, grammar.</i>

14
00:02:01.663 --> 00:02:05.334
<i>I took their advice
and, I grew up.</i>

15
00:02:07.044 --> 00:02:09.546
<i>I forgot about being a child.</i>

16
00:02:10.506 --> 00:02:13.717
<i>Until something miraculous
happened.</i>

17
00:02:27.731 --> 00:02:30.901
THE LITTLE PRINCE
Translation and review by Angel.

18
00:02:38.075 --> 00:02:41.662
I have always wanted to find someone
to share my story with, but...

19
00:02:41.745 --> 00:02:43.664
I do not know... I...

20
00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:47.084
I guess this world just
got too grown-up.

21
00:02:50.087 --> 00:02:55.092
Good morning, let us recap today's
recap of today's market activity.

22
00:02:55.217 --> 00:02:57.970
Record-breaking numbers were
written down on pieces of paper.

23
00:02:58.136 --> 00:03:01.265
Taken to the bank, placed
in drawers and locked with keys.

24
00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.143
Backs straight.

25
00:03:05.644 --> 00:03:07.271
Listening attentively.

26
00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:08.856
Listening.

27
00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.817
No excessive blinking.

28
00:03:12.442 --> 00:03:14.111
Listening.

29
00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:16.572
Unexpected praise.

30
00:03:16.655 --> 00:03:19.783
Acknowledge and thank you.

31
00:03:20.576 --> 00:03:23.453
A real smile. Sweetie!
Show your teeth.

32
00:03:23.704 --> 00:03:25.831
Not too much.

33
00:03:26.415 --> 00:03:27.791
Good. Okay.

34
00:03:28.375 --> 00:03:29.710
Now remember...

35
00:03:29.793 --> 00:03:33.171
Statistics tell us that if the panel
is leaning toward acceptance.

36
00:03:33.255 --> 00:03:35.299
They will ask only
one question.

37
00:03:35.382 --> 00:03:36.425
The big question.

38
00:03:37.593 --> 00:03:39.928
Are you Werth Academy material?

39
00:03:41.179 --> 00:03:42.848
Yes. I am.

40
00:03:43.515 --> 00:03:45.976
Three things make me Werth
Academy material.

41
00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.818
Zero. One. Seven?

42
00:03:56.737 --> 00:03:57.779
Go.

43
00:04:18.675 --> 00:04:22.012
We have reviewed
your application.

44
00:04:22.112 --> 00:04:24.889
- Good!
- Thank you!

45
00:04:25.349 --> 00:04:26.934
We have reviewed your
transcription.

46
00:04:27.017 --> 00:04:29.186
Thank... You.

47
00:04:34.191 --> 00:04:35.400
We have read essay.

48
00:04:35.525 --> 00:04:38.445
"The transformed power
of zero on the button line."

49
00:04:38.528 --> 00:04:41.031
And the follow-up,
"Zero, still my hero".

50
00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.579
Yes. We do that everything
looks to be in place.

51
00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.876
We will ask you just one
question today.

52
00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.378
<i>The big question!</i>

53
00:04:54.544 --> 00:04:56.546
<i>"Are you Werth
Academy material?"</i>

54
00:04:58.048 --> 00:05:01.551
What will you be?
When you grow up?

55
00:05:03.887 --> 00:05:05.639
Yes. I am.

56
00:05:06.264 --> 00:05:08.600
Three things make me Werth
Academy material.

57
00:05:08.725 --> 00:05:09.768
No! No!

58
00:05:09.893 --> 00:05:12.104
One: Like Werth.
I am insensible.

59
00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:14.147
Two: Like Werth.
I am serious.

60
00:05:14.231 --> 00:05:16.233
- Stop.
- Three...

61
00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:17.901
Like Werth...

62
00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.904
My unwavering...

63
00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:22.906
Abort... Abort.

64
00:05:23.073 --> 00:05:25.575
Concerned... with...

65
00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:27.828
Lean...

66
00:05:31.581 --> 00:05:32.624
Thank you.

67
00:05:34.292 --> 00:05:35.460
Sweetie!

68
00:05:37.004 --> 00:05:41.133
WHAT WILL YOU WANT TO BE?
WHEN YOU GROW UP?

69
00:05:41.258 --> 00:05:42.592
ESSENTIAL.

70
00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:51.268
Apparently, they changed
the big question.

71
00:05:53.687 --> 00:05:55.272
I am sorry. Mum!

72
00:05:55.939 --> 00:05:57.274
Do not be.

73
00:05:57.774 --> 00:05:59.401
We will just have
to go to Plan B.

74
00:05:59.484 --> 00:06:00.569
"B"?

75
00:06:00.652 --> 00:06:02.571
You said Plan B
was impossible!

76
00:06:02.654 --> 00:06:04.054
That is why we went
with the Plan A.

77
00:06:04.531 --> 00:06:06.533
Plan B is the new Plan A.

78
00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:09.661
We are moving forward!

79
00:06:11.496 --> 00:06:12.914
<i>Neighborhood identified.
Check.</i>

80
00:06:12.998 --> 00:06:16.418
<i>If by some miracle. We can find
a house in the neighborhood here.</i>

81
00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:18.381
<I>You are looking for.
They may have to take care.</I>

82
00:06:18.712 --> 00:06:20.464
REDUCED PRICE HOUSE FOR SALE

83
00:06:21.965 --> 00:06:23.341
<I>Check. Check.</I>

84
00:06:24.886 --> 00:06:27.804
<I>Check. Moving truck. Check.</I>

85
00:06:28.305 --> 00:06:29.598
FIRST DAY OF SUMMER HOLIDAYS

86
00:06:29.681 --> 00:06:32.309
<I>Matters of consequence today for
the serious and sensible man.</I>

87
00:06:32.476 --> 00:06:33.810
We did it!

88
00:06:33.977 --> 00:06:36.813
You are going to Werth Academy.
Whether they like it or not.

89
00:06:37.189 --> 00:06:41.151
<i>Whether volcanoes are extinct or
alive. It is equivalent for us.</i>

90
00:06:43.487 --> 00:06:46.990
<I>No one is ever satisfied
Where he is, pursuing nothing.</I>

91
00:06:50.327 --> 00:06:52.996
Our new home. Check.

92
00:07:11.848 --> 00:07:14.726
Is it too late for a Plan C?

93
00:07:15.185 --> 00:07:20.774
Just keep reminding yourself that
house made this house available.

94
00:07:21.191 --> 00:07:23.235
And, made your future possible.

95
00:07:41.753 --> 00:07:42.879
Mom?

96
00:07:49.886 --> 00:07:52.472
Do you really think?
I am Werth Academy material.

97
00:07:52.556 --> 00:07:55.976
You will be by the end of the
summer. Because I design the plan.

98
00:07:57.561 --> 00:07:58.603
Right on time.

99
00:08:00.605 --> 00:08:03.316
I present your life plan.

100
00:08:03.567 --> 00:08:04.776
Life plan?

101
00:08:08.155 --> 00:08:09.698
Life plan.

102
00:08:09.781 --> 00:08:12.492
We are not leaving
anything to chance.

103
00:08:12.576 --> 00:08:15.579
Everything is here. Or, end of
top to bottom. Left to right.

104
00:08:16.121 --> 00:08:17.281
Let us to take a closer look.

105
00:08:17.455 --> 00:08:20.125
The minute of the hour. Hour
of the day. Day of the week.

106
00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.461
Week of the month, month of the
year, the year of your life.

107
00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:25.589
Everything! You got it?

108
00:08:29.593 --> 00:08:32.012
It even got a chart for
all your birthday gifts.

109
00:08:32.095 --> 00:08:34.681
Like your ninth birthday,
coming up. Microscope.

110
00:08:34.764 --> 00:08:37.267
Perfect for the Werth
Academy biology curriculum.

111
00:08:37.475 --> 00:08:38.977
It already wrapped.

112
00:08:39.102 --> 00:08:41.146
- Wow!
- Yes. Wow!

113
00:08:41.438 --> 00:08:44.482
But, for now. All your
attention is upstairs.

114
00:08:44.941 --> 00:08:46.943
The first day of your new school.

115
00:08:48.111 --> 00:08:51.323
We got 53 days to go.
Which does not sound like much?

116
00:08:51.448 --> 00:08:54.492
Until you break it.
Into hours, 1.272.

117
00:08:54.618 --> 00:08:57.162
Or, minutes, 76, 320.

118
00:08:57.454 --> 00:09:00.624
Only then do you realize.
How much can be accomplished.

119
00:09:00.707 --> 00:09:04.377
You will use every minute,
hour and day according to this.

120
00:09:04.461 --> 00:09:06.463
Because, let us face it.

121
00:09:06.963 --> 00:09:08.965
You are going to be
all alone out there.

122
00:09:10.342 --> 00:09:11.509
All alone.

123
00:09:13.637 --> 00:09:15.222
So...

124
00:09:15.305 --> 00:09:17.682
We cannot afford any more
mistakes, like the interview.

125
00:09:17.807 --> 00:09:18.808
Right.

126
00:09:19.851 --> 00:09:23.230
You are going to make a
wonderful grown-up.

127
00:09:23.313 --> 00:09:24.689
Thank you. Mum.

128
00:09:26.483 --> 00:09:30.320
I wish I could stay. Sweetie,
but, it is the Davis audit, again.

129
00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:32.989
Kelly's numbers on the Miller
accounts are problematic.

130
00:09:33.073 --> 00:09:35.909
Fines found out and now
Logan is in a panic.

131
00:09:36.368 --> 00:09:37.410
Fisher wants nothing
to do with it.

132
00:09:37.494 --> 00:09:38.536
Logan.

133
00:09:38.662 --> 00:09:40.956
- So. I have gone in...
- And get balance out.

134
00:09:41.039 --> 00:09:43.750
Yes, but I am not even sure
that is possible.

135
00:09:43.917 --> 00:09:46.753
If anyone can do it.
It is you. You go!

136
00:09:46.836 --> 00:09:48.505
I got the life plan!

137
00:09:48.838 --> 00:09:50.674
You are my senior VP.

138
00:10:02.185 --> 00:10:03.186
Okay.

139
00:10:38.054 --> 00:10:39.055
Gas.

140
00:11:03.054 --> 00:11:04.055
No! No!

141
00:11:24.309 --> 00:11:26.644
<i>Anybody home?</i>

142
00:11:32.359 --> 00:11:33.943
<i>Bolts...</i>

143
00:11:52.379 --> 00:11:54.714
I did at actually believe,
He had a plane back there.

144
00:11:54.798 --> 00:11:57.634
I think the old person flew
away years ago.

145
00:11:57.717 --> 00:12:00.470
I am just thankful.
We do not live next door to him.

146
00:12:02.138 --> 00:12:03.306
Copy that.

147
00:12:12.649 --> 00:12:13.983
Hello there!

148
00:12:15.819 --> 00:12:17.737
A very good afternoon
to you, Officer.

149
00:12:17.862 --> 00:12:19.531
Friends!

150
00:12:25.829 --> 00:12:29.207
I was just... I immersed
in a game of bridge.

151
00:12:29.833 --> 00:12:31.000
Do you play?

152
00:12:36.005 --> 00:12:40.510
Sir. Did you try to start
your plane again?

153
00:12:44.264 --> 00:12:46.099
Yes! Yes I did.

154
00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:49.394
I am terribly sorry.
I am terribly sorry!

155
00:12:49.727 --> 00:12:53.565
I do believe I have caused extensive
damage to the house next door.

156
00:12:54.858 --> 00:12:56.192
Handcuffs?

157
00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:58.278
I would rather not.

158
00:12:58.528 --> 00:12:59.863
Hold on.

159
00:13:02.782 --> 00:13:05.118
<i>I know it is here
in somewhere.</i>

160
00:13:06.244 --> 00:13:07.412
<i>What?</i>

161
00:13:10.248 --> 00:13:11.624
I find it.

162
00:13:13.042 --> 00:13:14.252
Found it!

163
00:13:15.628 --> 00:13:16.713
Sir...

164
00:13:28.391 --> 00:13:30.935
Hey! I am home.
I brought Chinese.

165
00:13:31.227 --> 00:13:32.604
Mom?

166
00:13:32.729 --> 00:13:33.730
Hi?

167
00:13:34.564 --> 00:13:36.107
Hi.

168
00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:40.945
Where did you get the pennies?

169
00:13:41.738 --> 00:13:43.239
The old man next door.

170
00:13:45.074 --> 00:13:48.995
Actually, it was the police
officer who "gave" them to me.

171
00:13:49.621 --> 00:13:50.747
What?

172
00:13:53.833 --> 00:13:58.505
What kind of a nut keeps an airplane?
Actually, starts it in his backyard.

173
00:13:59.088 --> 00:14:00.757
Honey! Are you sure?
You are okay.

174
00:14:02.091 --> 00:14:03.885
- I have to call the insurance.
- Done.

175
00:14:03.968 --> 00:14:06.346
- And file a place report.
- Done. In duplicate.

176
00:14:06.429 --> 00:14:08.723
- Photo documentation?
- Inside and outside.

177
00:14:08.806 --> 00:14:10.808
The lighting could
have been better.

178
00:14:12.018 --> 00:14:13.019
It is not so bad.

179
00:14:19.442 --> 00:14:24.197
I will call a contractor in the morning
and, we will forget old man even exists.

180
00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:25.782
Forgot him.

181
00:14:26.491 --> 00:14:28.201
<I>Matters of consequence.</I>

182
00:14:28.618 --> 00:14:31.746
<I>Let us recap today's recap,
Of today is market activity.</I>

183
00:14:31.829 --> 00:14:34.791
<I>With a detailed account...
Numbers of the day.</I>

184
00:14:45.677 --> 00:14:47.804
<I>There are also
hundreds of others.</I>

185
00:15:33.516 --> 00:15:37.478
"Once upon a time there was a little
Prince who lived on a planet."

186
00:15:37.562 --> 00:15:41.899
"That was scarcely bigger than
himself, and who had need of..."

187
00:15:42.025 --> 00:15:43.026
A friend?

188
00:15:43.526 --> 00:15:45.403
<i>I thought you could
use a friend!</I>

189
00:15:46.863 --> 00:15:49.282
<I>No. Here I am, up here.</I>

190
00:15:50.033 --> 00:15:52.201
Yeah! Here! Hi?

191
00:15:54.203 --> 00:15:57.624
I am sorry. That is just
the beginning of the story.

192
00:15:57.707 --> 00:16:00.251
<I>It is okay. Nobody understands
it anyway.</I>

193
00:16:00.877 --> 00:16:02.211
<I>All right. Good-bye.</I>

194
00:16:02.629 --> 00:16:04.589
<I>See you later, maybe.</I>

195
00:16:11.929 --> 00:16:13.473
<I>She made the most
frightful noise.</I>

196
00:16:13.556 --> 00:16:15.433
<I>It resounded all over
the place.</I>

197
00:16:23.483 --> 00:16:26.736
- Maybe during lunch...
- I can raise those pennies.

198
00:17:45.483 --> 00:17:46.483
Ouch!

199
00:18:57.720 --> 00:19:00.973
Once upon time
there was a little prince.

200
00:19:01.057 --> 00:19:04.268
Who lived on a planet that
was scarcely bigger than him.

201
00:19:04.393 --> 00:19:06.062
And, who had need of a friend.

202
00:19:23.079 --> 00:19:26.749
"And lived my life alone without
anyone I could really talk to."

203
00:19:27.166 --> 00:19:29.669
"So I learned to
pilot aero planes."

204
00:19:46.936 --> 00:19:49.355
<I>I flew more or less all
over the world.</I>

205
00:19:49.438 --> 00:19:52.942
<I>Until had an accident
in the Sahara desert.</I>

206
00:20:59.008 --> 00:21:03.054
<I>If you please,
draw me a sheep!</I>

207
00:21:06.849 --> 00:21:09.226
If you please, draw me a sheep.

208
00:21:17.026 --> 00:21:18.694
Draw me a sheep!

209
00:21:19.195 --> 00:21:23.449
When a mystery is too
over-powering. No wonder disobey.

210
00:21:24.367 --> 00:21:26.535
Draw? I do not know
how to draw.

211
00:21:27.411 --> 00:21:28.871
That does not matter.

212
00:21:31.624 --> 00:21:33.960
<i>The first sheep I drew
was too sickly.</i>

213
00:21:35.461 --> 00:21:38.047
<i>And the second one,
not to his liking either.</i>

214
00:21:39.215 --> 00:21:41.175
<i>You do not see that
this is not a sheep.</i>

215
00:21:41.258 --> 00:21:43.636
<i>This is a ram, it has horns.</i>

216
00:21:43.719 --> 00:21:46.889
<I>- And this one was...
- Too old!</I>

217
00:21:49.725 --> 00:21:53.229
I want a sheep that
will live for a long time.

218
00:21:56.565 --> 00:21:58.234
<I>So, I drew this.</I>

219
00:22:02.154 --> 00:22:03.906
The sheep you ask
for is inside.

220
00:22:05.825 --> 00:22:07.827
That exactly the way
I wanted it.

221
00:22:10.329 --> 00:22:13.174
Do you think this sheep will
eat a great deal of grass?

222
00:22:13.250 --> 00:22:16.585
Because where I live,
everything is very small.

223
00:22:17.461 --> 00:22:19.880
I am sure there will be
enough grass for him.

224
00:22:19.964 --> 00:22:21.424
He is a very small sheep.

225
00:22:21.590 --> 00:22:24.552
Not that small. Look!
He is gone to sleep.

226
00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:10.306
Wow!

227
00:23:40.503 --> 00:23:41.837
Hello?

228
00:23:52.306 --> 00:23:53.349
Hello?

229
00:23:54.183 --> 00:23:55.309
Hello?

230
00:24:04.193 --> 00:24:06.028
Hold on. Do not move.

231
00:24:10.658 --> 00:24:12.034
Damn it!

232
00:24:12.368 --> 00:24:13.702
Here we go.

233
00:24:15.538 --> 00:24:16.580
Wow!

234
00:24:39.061 --> 00:24:42.773
I...I just wanted to give
you are drawing back.

235
00:24:43.899 --> 00:24:44.942
You do not like it.

236
00:24:45.067 --> 00:24:46.861
No! I did.

237
00:24:47.361 --> 00:24:48.404
It is not very good.

238
00:24:48.571 --> 00:24:49.822
I think it is nice.

239
00:24:49.905 --> 00:24:52.408
I read the story, too.
Attentively.

240
00:24:53.117 --> 00:24:55.911
And, I found it quite odd.

241
00:24:56.704 --> 00:24:57.746
Odd?

242
00:24:57.872 --> 00:25:00.541
I mean curious...
or, interesting...

243
00:25:00.749 --> 00:25:03.085
I have some issues
with some of the facts.

244
00:25:04.086 --> 00:25:05.171
You have questions.

245
00:25:05.254 --> 00:25:07.590
I do not mean to be rude.
Can I?

246
00:25:07.756 --> 00:25:10.259
Be rude! Sure, go ahead.
What you got.

247
00:25:10.759 --> 00:25:14.430
First, what was the kid
doing there in the desert?

248
00:25:14.555 --> 00:25:15.556
It is very strange.

249
00:25:15.639 --> 00:25:18.809
No one can last very long in
a desert without food and water.

250
00:25:18.976 --> 00:25:21.770
Where are his parents?
Does he even go to school?

251
00:25:21.937 --> 00:25:24.607
Does he really live up there?
I took basic astronomy.

252
00:25:24.732 --> 00:25:28.444
And, there was no mention of life,
or, children on any other planets.

253
00:25:28.569 --> 00:25:31.447
Unless it is, true that
he came from a star.

254
00:25:31.572 --> 00:25:32.615
That is improbably.

255
00:25:32.823 --> 00:25:35.576
Not a star. An asteroid.

256
00:25:36.118 --> 00:25:38.204
Asteroid B-612.

257
00:25:38.287 --> 00:25:41.123
We did not cover asteroids.

258
00:25:41.916 --> 00:25:46.253
But the fact that he wanted a sheep,
that pretty much proves that he exists.

259
00:25:46.754 --> 00:25:48.297
Do not you think?

260
00:25:55.304 --> 00:25:58.140
Hold on. I will show you
another drawing.

261
00:26:03.479 --> 00:26:04.605
Wow!

262
00:26:05.689 --> 00:26:08.192
This is a pretty
serious fire hazard.

263
00:26:08.317 --> 00:26:10.819
I never looked at that way.

264
00:26:10.986 --> 00:26:12.529
Where did you get
all this stuff?

265
00:26:12.988 --> 00:26:17.368
<i>Well! As you live somethings
just kind to stick to you.</i>

266
00:26:18.160 --> 00:26:20.037
<i>There is a name for that...</i>

267
00:26:20.454 --> 00:26:21.538
- Collecting?
- Hoarding!

268
00:26:21.830 --> 00:26:23.332
I said: Hoarding.

269
00:26:23.666 --> 00:26:26.210
I am a hoarder.
A bit of a hoarder.

270
00:26:30.339 --> 00:26:32.007
What is your name, little Fox?

271
00:26:32.675 --> 00:26:34.385
He cannot answer you.

272
00:26:34.510 --> 00:26:37.137
I keep meaning
to sew him a mouth.

273
00:26:50.359 --> 00:26:53.112
Are you okay?

274
00:26:53.195 --> 00:26:55.698
I am fine. This happens
sometimes.

275
00:26:56.198 --> 00:26:57.408
Give me a minute.

276
00:26:57.533 --> 00:27:00.577
The last time this happened.
I was down here for three days.

277
00:27:00.703 --> 00:27:02.079
- Three days?
- That is okay.

278
00:27:02.204 --> 00:27:06.000
That is why I always keep
a sandwich in my pocket.

279
00:27:06.083 --> 00:27:07.543
Do you want a bite a baloney?

280
00:27:08.335 --> 00:27:11.005
I think I am baloney intolerant.

281
00:27:11.672 --> 00:27:13.257
Do you think is baloney?

282
00:27:18.012 --> 00:27:20.347
It will be a clear night.

283
00:27:29.273 --> 00:27:31.400
They will be out soon.

284
00:27:33.027 --> 00:27:34.236
Wow!

285
00:27:37.406 --> 00:27:41.535
The Little Prince. He was very
fond of sunsets.

286
00:27:41.910 --> 00:27:44.747
One day he saw 44.

287
00:27:45.414 --> 00:27:46.457
What?

288
00:27:46.582 --> 00:27:48.751
His planet, it was so small.

289
00:27:48.876 --> 00:27:52.755
All he had to do was his chair
a few steps to see another one.

290
00:27:54.256 --> 00:27:57.593
But a small planet also
had drawbacks.

291
00:27:58.052 --> 00:28:01.388
He needed a sheep to eat
the baobab sprouts.

292
00:28:01.764 --> 00:28:03.140
- Baobab?
- Yeah!

293
00:28:03.265 --> 00:28:05.100
It is very greedy tree.

294
00:28:05.976 --> 00:28:10.814
<I>And every day, he toiled
to stop them from turning up.</I>

295
00:28:11.440 --> 00:28:13.108
<I>For it, He intervenes too late..</I>

296
00:28:13.650 --> 00:28:15.319
Catastrophe.

297
00:28:15.986 --> 00:28:18.947
<i>Now, luckily, there are
good seeds, too.</i>

298
00:28:19.281 --> 00:28:23.827
<i>And one day, from a seed blown
no one knew know where.</i>

299
00:28:24.244 --> 00:28:27.247
<I>A new kind of sprout show up.</I>

300
00:28:35.172 --> 00:28:37.216
I know you will be
miraculous.

301
00:28:37.299 --> 00:28:38.967
I know you will.

302
00:28:55.150 --> 00:28:57.194
How beautiful you are!

303
00:28:57.361 --> 00:28:58.821
I am only half-awake.

304
00:28:59.321 --> 00:29:01.490
Forgive me. I am still
quite disheveled.

305
00:29:01.657 --> 00:29:02.950
You are perfect.

306
00:29:03.617 --> 00:29:04.660
Am I not?

307
00:29:05.327 --> 00:29:08.205
I was born at the same
moment as the sun.

308
00:29:13.460 --> 00:29:17.464
<i>It was there they shared
their first sunrise.</i>

309
00:29:19.007 --> 00:29:21.677
<i>And their first sunset.</i>

310
00:29:23.512 --> 00:29:25.556
It is very cold
where you live.

311
00:29:32.146 --> 00:29:34.731
If you have the kindness
to think of my needs.

312
00:29:35.524 --> 00:29:39.027
<i>But the Rose began very quickly
to torment him with her vanity.</i>

313
00:29:39.153 --> 00:29:41.321
I suppose you would not
have a screen?

314
00:29:41.488 --> 00:29:44.158
And, at night, I want you
to put me under a glass.

315
00:29:44.324 --> 00:29:46.034
A glass, now. My needs...

316
00:29:46.160 --> 00:29:47.369
My screen...

317
00:29:47.870 --> 00:29:51.248
<i>Now, the shame of it was
that they loved each other.</i>

318
00:29:51.874 --> 00:29:55.878
<i>But they were both too
young to know how to love.</i>

319
00:29:58.005 --> 00:30:01.049
<i>Full of doubt. He ran away.</i>

320
00:30:02.384 --> 00:30:03.927
Of course! I love you.

321
00:30:04.511 --> 00:30:06.680
If you are not aware of that.
It is my fault.

322
00:30:06.847 --> 00:30:08.056
Please forgive me.

323
00:30:17.274 --> 00:30:19.401
He left her. All alone!

324
00:30:20.068 --> 00:30:21.904
But, where did he go?

325
00:30:22.362 --> 00:30:24.781
Well! He did not know
it at the time.

326
00:30:24.907 --> 00:30:28.452
But, his leaving was just the first
step on a journey back to her.

327
00:30:28.744 --> 00:30:30.245
- Really?
- Yeah!

328
00:30:31.205 --> 00:30:33.749
Look at that,
the stars are out.

329
00:30:40.422 --> 00:30:41.423
Wow!

330
00:30:42.257 --> 00:30:43.592
They are so bright!

331
00:30:44.885 --> 00:30:47.137
There are so many to look at.

332
00:30:47.930 --> 00:30:51.517
And on a good day,
if I listen carefully.

333
00:30:51.600 --> 00:30:53.936
I can hear him
laughing up there.

334
00:31:08.784 --> 00:31:10.452
No! I do not know!

335
00:31:19.962 --> 00:31:22.297
<i>Sweetie? Where are you?</i>

336
00:31:27.469 --> 00:31:28.470
Hi.

337
00:31:29.012 --> 00:31:32.516
Your desk is a mess. Did you
finish your study work for today?

338
00:31:34.268 --> 00:31:36.728
Not exactly.

339
00:31:36.812 --> 00:31:38.647
What have you been doing?

340
00:31:39.690 --> 00:31:41.316
I read a lot.

341
00:31:41.984 --> 00:31:43.819
And, I made a friend.

342
00:31:45.654 --> 00:31:46.655
A friend?

343
00:31:47.322 --> 00:31:50.951
No. No. No. No.

344
00:31:51.493 --> 00:31:53.161
No!

345
00:31:53.829 --> 00:31:55.163
Maybe...

346
00:31:56.790 --> 00:31:58.000
Yes.

347
00:31:58.125 --> 00:31:59.167
Okay.

348
00:32:01.837 --> 00:32:02.963
FRIEND

349
00:32:03.046 --> 00:32:06.592
If you study hard and you stay
completely on track with the plan.

350
00:32:06.675 --> 00:32:09.553
You can spend some time
with your new friend.

351
00:32:09.678 --> 00:32:12.723
Nest summer, on Thursday
from 1:00 to 1:30.

352
00:32:13.307 --> 00:32:15.642
Okay? I cannot wait to meet her.

353
00:32:27.696 --> 00:32:30.157
"He found himself in the
neighborhood of asteroids."

354
00:32:30.240 --> 00:32:34.411
"325. 326. 327."

355
00:32:34.911 --> 00:32:39.541
<I>"328. 329. 330."</I>

356
00:32:42.586 --> 00:32:44.880
What?

357
00:32:45.213 --> 00:32:46.882
Here is a subject.

358
00:32:47.341 --> 00:32:48.842
Approach.

359
00:32:48.925 --> 00:32:51.053
Sire. Over what do you rule?

360
00:32:51.386 --> 00:32:53.221
Over everything.

361
00:32:53.764 --> 00:32:55.474
And, the stars obey you?

362
00:32:55.557 --> 00:32:59.227
They certainly do. I do not
permit insubordination.

363
00:33:00.562 --> 00:33:03.357
I would very much
like to see a sunset.

364
00:33:03.440 --> 00:33:05.984
It would remind me my Rose.

365
00:33:06.068 --> 00:33:08.070
Could you order the sun to set?

366
00:33:12.532 --> 00:33:14.368
You shall have your sunset.

367
00:33:14.451 --> 00:33:16.119
I shall command it.

368
00:33:16.411 --> 00:33:19.414
But I shall wait the
conditions are favorable.

369
00:33:19.706 --> 00:33:20.791
When will that be?

370
00:33:22.417 --> 00:33:24.336
Well! That will be about...
About...

371
00:33:24.419 --> 00:33:29.466
That will be this evening.
About 20 minutes to 8:00.

372
00:33:35.597 --> 00:33:37.099
Good morning.

373
00:33:37.265 --> 00:33:39.226
You are wearing a funny
kind of hat.

374
00:33:39.309 --> 00:33:44.064
What... It is a hat for
salutes actually.

375
00:33:44.147 --> 00:33:46.608
To raise when people
acclaim me.

376
00:33:48.110 --> 00:33:50.278
Clap your hands. Yeah.

377
00:33:51.738 --> 00:33:53.615
Thank you. Thank you.

378
00:33:53.740 --> 00:33:54.991
You see!

379
00:33:58.328 --> 00:34:02.249
Do you really admire
me very much?

380
00:34:03.333 --> 00:34:07.129
Am I the handsomest?
The best dressed. The richest...

381
00:34:07.796 --> 00:34:10.465
Am I the most intelligent
man on this planet?

382
00:34:11.466 --> 00:34:14.302
But, you are the only
man on this planet.

383
00:34:16.138 --> 00:34:17.806
Do me this kindness and...

384
00:34:18.432 --> 00:34:21.435
Admire me just the same.
Please?

385
00:34:24.855 --> 00:34:26.857
<I>I own the stars.</I>

386
00:34:27.023 --> 00:34:28.817
<I>I minister them.</I>

387
00:34:28.942 --> 00:34:30.652
I count them.
Then I recount them.

388
00:34:31.027 --> 00:34:33.321
But, what good does
that does you.

389
00:34:33.488 --> 00:34:37.075
Well! It is good to make me rich.
How is that?

390
00:34:37.159 --> 00:34:39.953
And, what good does it
do you to be rich?

391
00:34:40.287 --> 00:34:43.165
It makes it possible for me
to buy more stars.

392
00:34:43.498 --> 00:34:46.209
Plus anything else
you can think of.

393
00:34:48.503 --> 00:34:52.674
Grown-ups are certainly
very, very odd.

394
00:34:54.676 --> 00:34:58.847
And, check. And, check.
And, check.

395
00:35:00.140 --> 00:35:01.183
Check.

396
00:35:01.683 --> 00:35:02.809
Check.

397
00:35:03.727 --> 00:35:06.021
And, check. And, check.

398
00:35:06.646 --> 00:35:09.645
Check... Check... Check.

399
00:35:09.646 --> 00:35:13.649
Check... Check... Check.

400
00:35:14.196 --> 00:35:19.201
Grown-ups are certainly
very, very odd.

401
00:35:19.701 --> 00:35:21.828
I have lived a great deal
among grown-ups.

402
00:35:22.496 --> 00:35:24.331
I have seen then up close.

403
00:35:24.414 --> 00:35:26.917
And, that has not much changed
my opinion of them.

404
00:35:27.375 --> 00:35:31.004
I am not so sure.
I want to grow up anymore.

405
00:35:31.379 --> 00:35:33.340
Growing up is not the problem.

406
00:35:33.924 --> 00:35:35.217
Forgetting it.

407
00:35:36.218 --> 00:35:38.720
I definitely do not
want to forget.

408
00:35:39.054 --> 00:35:42.891
I managed grow up and I never
forgot the Little Prince.

409
00:35:50.899 --> 00:35:51.942
Yeah...

410
00:36:21.221 --> 00:36:22.430
Good evening!

411
00:36:26.434 --> 00:36:27.602
Good evening!

412
00:36:27.727 --> 00:36:29.145
What planet is this?

413
00:36:29.896 --> 00:36:31.356
This is Earth.

414
00:36:31.439 --> 00:36:32.607
This is Africa.

415
00:36:34.276 --> 00:36:35.735
Where are all the men?

416
00:36:35.944 --> 00:36:38.280
It is a little lonely
in the desert.

417
00:36:38.405 --> 00:36:40.574
It is also lonely among men.

418
00:36:41.449 --> 00:36:45.785
You are a funny animal.
You are no thicker than a finger.

419
00:36:46.329 --> 00:36:49.624
But, I am more powerful
than the finger of a king.

420
00:36:50.458 --> 00:36:51.751
You have not any feet.

421
00:36:52.252 --> 00:36:54.004
You cannot even travel.

422
00:36:54.129 --> 00:36:57.507
I can carry you further than
any ship can take you.

423
00:37:01.136 --> 00:37:04.556
I can help you someday,
if you go to your own planet.

424
00:37:04.639 --> 00:37:07.350
I think I understand you.

425
00:37:11.479 --> 00:37:15.025
There you go, try that one
on the left there.

426
00:37:17.319 --> 00:37:18.653
I am scared.

427
00:37:19.112 --> 00:37:20.989
That is normal. It is scary.

428
00:37:21.489 --> 00:37:23.783
Why do you think I sent you?

429
00:37:26.536 --> 00:37:28.872
Almost there. You got it now.

430
00:37:29.706 --> 00:37:31.333
Just reach! Reach for it!

431
00:37:32.834 --> 00:37:35.170
- I got it!
- There you go! You got it!

432
00:37:41.885 --> 00:37:44.054
Well! That was...

433
00:37:44.346 --> 00:37:46.139
That was doubling scary. Yeah?

434
00:37:47.140 --> 00:37:48.892
Triple and quadruple.

435
00:37:49.017 --> 00:37:51.353
That not to amputate.

436
00:37:52.062 --> 00:37:53.146
What?

437
00:37:59.027 --> 00:38:01.196
- Feels better?
- Yeah.

438
00:38:11.247 --> 00:38:15.168
<i>But it happened that after
walking a long time through sand.</i>

439
00:38:15.710 --> 00:38:17.212
<i>And rocks, and snow.</i>

440
00:38:17.587 --> 00:38:19.381
<I>The Fox appeared.</I>

441
00:38:31.726 --> 00:38:33.687
Hey! Come play with me.

442
00:38:34.396 --> 00:38:36.398
I cannot play with you.

443
00:38:36.773 --> 00:38:38.066
I am not tame.

444
00:38:38.274 --> 00:38:39.776
What does that mean?

445
00:38:40.902 --> 00:38:42.904
Tame means: "To establish ties."

446
00:38:43.363 --> 00:38:45.699
To me. You are still nothing
more than a little boy.

447
00:38:45.782 --> 00:38:48.451
Who is just like 100.000
other little boys.

448
00:38:49.244 --> 00:38:50.870
And, I have no need of you.

449
00:38:50.954 --> 00:38:52.288
And, you have no need of me.

450
00:38:53.081 --> 00:38:56.793
To you. I am not more a Fox
like 100.000 Foxes.

451
00:38:57.419 --> 00:39:00.422
But if you tame me,
then we shall need each other.

452
00:39:20.150 --> 00:39:21.609
Hey! There.

453
00:40:29.094 --> 00:40:31.846
To me, you will be unique
in the entire world.

454
00:40:32.013 --> 00:40:34.974
And, to you, I shall be
unique in the entire world.

455
00:41:26.860 --> 00:41:27.902
Who are you?

456
00:41:28.027 --> 00:41:31.238
We are Roses. We are Roses.
We are Roses.

457
00:41:32.740 --> 00:41:35.743
My Rose is just
a common Rose?

458
00:41:36.578 --> 00:41:40.331
But, told me. She was the only one
of her kind in the whole universe.

459
00:41:41.749 --> 00:41:43.751
But, she is not a common Rose.

460
00:41:43.918 --> 00:41:45.003
She is your Rose.

461
00:41:45.753 --> 00:41:49.340
The time that you have devoted to
she makes your Rose so important.

462
00:41:50.550 --> 00:41:52.177
She is my Rose.

463
00:41:53.261 --> 00:41:54.596
You must return to her.

464
00:42:01.936 --> 00:42:04.397
No! You gone cry.

465
00:42:05.773 --> 00:42:08.735
My taming have done
you no good at all.

466
00:42:13.072 --> 00:42:15.200
Let me make you a
present another a secret.

467
00:42:15.621 --> 00:42:22.373
That only with the heart
that one can see rightly.

468
00:42:22.707 --> 00:42:26.085
<i>What is essential is
invisible to the eye.</i>

469
00:42:29.964 --> 00:42:31.549
They will not be together
anymore?

470
00:42:33.301 --> 00:42:34.427
But, they will.

471
00:42:35.470 --> 00:42:39.140
The Fox. He sees the Little Prince
when he looks with his heart.

472
00:42:39.641 --> 00:42:42.810
If you can do that.
You will never be lonely again.

473
00:42:43.478 --> 00:42:47.065
Right. But, I am not lonely.
I have you now.

474
00:42:47.982 --> 00:42:49.651
I am so lucky.

475
00:42:49.776 --> 00:42:53.404
I thought I would never find anyone
who wanted to hear my story.

476
00:42:53.488 --> 00:42:56.449
Then you came along.
Just in time.

477
00:42:58.243 --> 00:42:59.327
Wait...

478
00:43:00.578 --> 00:43:02.830
What do you mean?
"Just in time."

479
00:43:05.833 --> 00:43:11.005
Well! Everyone has to say
goodbye soon or later.

480
00:43:12.173 --> 00:43:13.341
You are leaving.

481
00:43:14.008 --> 00:43:15.593
Well!

482
00:43:15.677 --> 00:43:19.305
What if I get that
old plane running?

483
00:43:20.139 --> 00:43:21.849
What if it is time for me.

484
00:43:22.642 --> 00:43:25.270
To go be with the Little Prince.

485
00:43:26.354 --> 00:43:27.438
But...

486
00:43:27.939 --> 00:43:29.524
He already has his Rose...

487
00:43:30.775 --> 00:43:32.610
And, I need you here.

488
00:43:39.701 --> 00:43:41.160
Hey! Hey!

489
00:43:42.328 --> 00:43:43.371
You are hungry.

490
00:43:43.955 --> 00:43:45.206
I know a great place.

491
00:43:45.331 --> 00:43:48.376
Where we can get free
pancakes on your birthday.

492
00:43:48.876 --> 00:43:51.296
But, my birthday is not
for two weeks.

493
00:43:51.629 --> 00:43:52.880
They do not know that.

494
00:44:01.723 --> 00:44:03.891
It is like flying a plane.

495
00:44:06.978 --> 00:44:08.730
Like the one you crashed.

496
00:44:08.813 --> 00:44:10.064
Exactly!

497
00:44:54.776 --> 00:44:56.694
What?

498
00:45:06.287 --> 00:45:08.122
Pull over.

499
00:45:20.093 --> 00:45:21.803
Do you have driver's license?

500
00:45:21.886 --> 00:45:22.970
No.

501
00:45:24.097 --> 00:45:25.723
- A learner's permit?
- No.

502
00:45:25.807 --> 00:45:26.974
How old are you?

503
00:45:27.058 --> 00:45:30.478
- Hi! Officer.
- You obvious set your car. Again.

504
00:45:30.603 --> 00:45:31.979
Yeah...

505
00:45:32.063 --> 00:45:35.775
Good afternoon. Officer.
If I may interject for a moment...

506
00:45:36.067 --> 00:45:38.319
Did you know it is my birthday?

507
00:45:42.657 --> 00:45:44.409
- Mom. I can...
- Wait for me inside.

508
00:45:44.492 --> 00:45:45.827
- But...
- Now!

509
00:45:47.995 --> 00:45:50.164
<i>Ma'am. I am very sorry to call
you at work.</i>

510
00:45:50.331 --> 00:45:53.167
<i>Apparently, they were going
to get pancakes.</i>

511
00:45:55.461 --> 00:45:57.922
- Would you like to speak to him?
- Yes.

512
00:45:58.005 --> 00:46:00.967
No! No! No! No!

513
00:46:09.809 --> 00:46:11.602
Mr. Fox!

514
00:46:13.187 --> 00:46:15.857
According to this.
You are still in bed.

515
00:46:15.982 --> 00:46:17.358
Asleep. Yesterday.

516
00:46:19.277 --> 00:46:22.029
Your "friend" does not even
have a driver's license.

517
00:46:22.155 --> 00:46:25.116
No. They took it away
after the fourth time.

518
00:46:25.199 --> 00:46:28.035
He drove away with
the gas pump attached.

519
00:46:30.121 --> 00:46:31.456
You could have been killing!

520
00:46:31.539 --> 00:46:34.459
- Mom! I can explain.
- No. No. You mean. You can lie.

521
00:46:34.542 --> 00:46:36.169
- But...
- You can lie to me.

522
00:46:36.294 --> 00:46:37.712
You lied to the police officer.

523
00:46:37.879 --> 00:46:40.339
Yes. Right! Before I forget.
Happy birthday.

524
00:46:41.966 --> 00:46:44.510
You even managed
to lie to your life plan!

525
00:46:44.886 --> 00:46:47.513
That? It is just a board
full of magnets!

526
00:46:47.638 --> 00:46:49.724
You mean care more about
that than about me.

527
00:46:49.807 --> 00:46:51.309
You are wrong.

528
00:46:51.559 --> 00:46:54.520
I care about it
as much as I care about you.

529
00:46:55.062 --> 00:46:56.397
Is you.

530
00:46:56.481 --> 00:47:00.234
This is your life and I am only one
taking any responsibility for it!

531
00:47:00.568 --> 00:47:04.071
That is your version of my life.
Not mine!

532
00:47:04.155 --> 00:47:06.991
If you ever around,
you would see that!

533
00:47:07.074 --> 00:47:10.411
You know very well.
Why I have to work so hard.

534
00:47:11.078 --> 00:47:12.914
Just like him now.

535
00:47:13.206 --> 00:47:15.333
Too busy. Always working.

536
00:47:15.750 --> 00:47:17.752
How long until you
completely disappear?

537
00:47:23.758 --> 00:47:26.427
"I believe that for his
escape he took advantage."

538
00:47:26.552 --> 00:47:29.263
"Of the migration of
a flock of wild birds."

539
00:47:29.764 --> 00:47:31.182
No! No!

540
00:47:31.349 --> 00:47:33.768
Okay! Enough of this nonsense.

541
00:47:33.893 --> 00:47:35.937
You have two weeks to focus
to where is essential.

542
00:47:36.062 --> 00:47:37.396
But... Mum!

543
00:49:08.529 --> 00:49:11.490
LOVE, DAD

544
00:49:52.573 --> 00:49:54.492
Let us look for a well.

545
00:50:30.111 --> 00:50:34.448
The stars are beautiful because
of a flower that cannot be seen.

546
00:50:41.288 --> 00:50:45.960
What makes the desert beautiful?
Is that somewhere it hides a well.

547
00:50:48.546 --> 00:50:53.467
<i>In the moonlight, I looked at his
pale forehead, his closed eyes.</i>

548
00:50:54.301 --> 00:50:56.804
<i>His locks of hair that trembled
in the wind.</i>

549
00:50:56.929 --> 00:50:58.639
<I>And I said to myself.</I>

550
00:50:58.764 --> 00:51:02.309
"What I see here is
nothing but a shell."

551
00:51:03.310 --> 00:51:07.231
"What most important
is one invisible."

552
00:51:19.952 --> 00:51:22.288
<i>We found a well at daybreak.</i>

553
00:51:29.253 --> 00:51:32.757
The men where you live
grow thousands of Roses.

554
00:51:32.840 --> 00:51:36.093
And, they do not find
what they are looking for.

555
00:51:37.678 --> 00:51:41.432
What they are looking for
could find in a single Rose.

556
00:51:41.515 --> 00:51:43.184
Or a little water.

557
00:52:14.715 --> 00:52:15.841
Hold your horses.

558
00:52:18.552 --> 00:52:20.721
Let us go look for a well.

559
00:52:21.138 --> 00:52:22.723
No. No. Listen.

560
00:52:23.057 --> 00:52:25.643
I made a big mistake
the other day.

561
00:52:26.227 --> 00:52:28.187
You cannot come over
here anymore.

562
00:52:28.395 --> 00:52:30.731
- It is okay! This will be the last time.
- What?

563
00:52:30.815 --> 00:52:33.067
Come on! Let us get
that plane running!

564
00:52:38.155 --> 00:52:41.158
I think If you managed to walk
to the desert finding a well.

565
00:52:41.242 --> 00:52:43.661
Then we can go and
find the Little Prince.

566
00:52:44.329 --> 00:52:47.039
He will be able to help us.

567
00:52:47.164 --> 00:52:50.918
Wait. Little what?
We cannot just take off.

568
00:52:51.710 --> 00:52:52.837
You are right.

569
00:52:52.920 --> 00:52:54.672
We can fix that wing first.

570
00:52:54.755 --> 00:52:56.048
No! No!

571
00:52:57.258 --> 00:53:02.179
I am sorry, but when the moment
does come for me to leave.

572
00:53:03.264 --> 00:53:04.849
I have to go alone.

573
00:53:06.767 --> 00:53:09.770
But, I will not be any trouble.

574
00:53:09.854 --> 00:53:12.606
And, I will not take up much
room in the plane. I promise.

575
00:53:13.107 --> 00:53:14.275
Do not go without me.

576
00:53:16.861 --> 00:53:20.197
I think it is time. I told you
the end of the story.

577
00:53:24.535 --> 00:53:29.707
<i>That evening. I finished my plane and
I went to find the Little Prince.</i>

578
00:53:29.790 --> 00:53:32.293
I shall be there tonight.
Wait for me.

579
00:53:32.751 --> 00:53:35.087
You are sure. I will not
suffer too long?

580
00:53:46.140 --> 00:53:47.224
Did you shoot it?

581
00:53:47.558 --> 00:53:49.977
No. It disappeared
among the stones.

582
00:53:50.269 --> 00:53:51.478
What happened?

583
00:53:52.313 --> 00:53:55.649
Somehow. He knew that
I had fixed my plane.

584
00:54:00.487 --> 00:54:02.990
I, too, am going back
home today.

585
00:54:03.115 --> 00:54:04.575
It is much farther.

586
00:54:04.658 --> 00:54:06.327
It is much more difficult.

587
00:54:07.953 --> 00:54:09.246
I am afraid.

588
00:54:13.667 --> 00:54:16.921
I cannot believe. I will never
hear you laugh again.

589
00:54:17.630 --> 00:54:19.673
I am going to make
you a present.

590
00:54:21.592 --> 00:54:24.303
In one of those stars.
I shall be living.

591
00:54:24.970 --> 00:54:27.139
In one of them.
I shall be laughing.

592
00:54:28.015 --> 00:54:30.643
And so, when you look up
at the sky at night.

593
00:54:30.935 --> 00:54:34.021
It will be as if all the
stars are laughing.

594
00:54:41.695 --> 00:54:43.781
Tonight. You do not come.

595
00:54:43.864 --> 00:54:46.951
Do you let him go?
Not the Snake!

596
00:54:48.202 --> 00:54:49.536
It was not my choice.

597
00:54:50.663 --> 00:54:52.456
<i>It was time to goodbye.</i>

598
00:54:54.708 --> 00:54:57.044
Do you understand
that it is too far.

599
00:54:57.211 --> 00:55:00.381
I cannot carry
this body with me.

600
00:55:00.881 --> 00:55:03.384
It will be like an old
abandoned shell.

601
00:55:03.801 --> 00:55:06.553
There is nothing sad
about old shells.

602
00:55:19.233 --> 00:55:22.194
- Here is the place.
- I shall not leave you.

603
00:55:48.971 --> 00:55:50.139
But...

604
00:55:51.849 --> 00:55:53.100
But...

605
00:56:00.774 --> 00:56:03.485
You said he is up there.
Did not you?

606
00:56:03.569 --> 00:56:04.820
Back his Rose.

607
00:56:04.903 --> 00:56:05.946
Well!

608
00:56:06.031 --> 00:56:08.615
It is as he said.

609
00:56:08.699 --> 00:56:11.535
I look at the stars
and, I hear him laughing.

610
00:56:12.202 --> 00:56:14.413
But, you do not know for sure.

611
00:56:15.497 --> 00:56:18.918
It would comfort me
very much if I know for sure.

612
00:56:19.127 --> 00:56:24.006
Instead, I choose to
believe he is up there.

613
00:56:27.843 --> 00:56:30.679
Is that you want me to do?
When you go.

614
00:56:31.013 --> 00:56:32.681
Just look up to the stars.

615
00:56:33.140 --> 00:56:35.642
And make-believe that
you are not gone.

616
00:56:36.185 --> 00:56:37.227
But...

617
00:56:37.644 --> 00:56:41.648
if you look with your heart.
I will always be with you.

618
00:56:42.024 --> 00:56:46.487
Yes. Just like, I know the Little
Prince will always be with his Rose.

619
00:56:46.904 --> 00:56:49.281
But, you cannot know for sure.

620
00:56:49.531 --> 00:56:52.117
What if he is not back
with his rose?

621
00:56:52.701 --> 00:56:54.661
- What if he is all grown up and alone?
- But...

622
00:56:54.787 --> 00:56:57.790
What if he's lost and
he has forgotten everything.

623
00:56:58.540 --> 00:57:01.251
What? Wait! Sweetheart.

624
00:57:01.335 --> 00:57:03.629
The Little Prince
will never forget.

625
00:57:03.712 --> 00:57:06.590
He will always be up there
for us. To help us.

626
00:57:07.049 --> 00:57:10.260
I do not want his help.
I hate the Little Prince!

627
00:57:10.344 --> 00:57:12.888
I wasted my whole summer,
on the Little Prince!

628
00:57:13.013 --> 00:57:16.308
I wish you had never told
me this stupid story.

629
00:57:49.133 --> 00:57:51.677
LAST DAY OF SUMMER HOLIDAYS

630
00:57:52.345 --> 00:57:57.432
<i>The weather caused 32
people to be late for work.</i>

631
00:57:57.516 --> 00:58:00.978
<i>Productivity decreased by 0,4%.</i>

632
00:58:09.570 --> 00:58:10.779
What?

633
00:58:11.071 --> 00:58:12.114
Dear!

634
00:58:20.664 --> 00:58:22.040
Honey! Where...

635
00:58:28.904 --> 00:58:29.981
No!

636
00:58:46.648 --> 00:58:47.941
Sweetie! Not!

637
00:58:54.489 --> 00:58:55.532
Hey!

638
00:59:10.505 --> 00:59:13.300
Sweetie! Stop!
What are you doing?

639
00:59:24.394 --> 00:59:26.813
Stop! You cannot go!

640
00:59:27.064 --> 00:59:29.149
Please? I need you here!

641
00:59:30.067 --> 00:59:30.901
No!

642
00:59:30.984 --> 00:59:33.862
Please! You have to let
I see him!

643
00:59:34.112 --> 00:59:36.490
What happened to him?
Is he going be okay?

644
00:59:44.706 --> 00:59:46.041
So...

645
00:59:47.292 --> 00:59:51.129
Let us not forget. Tomorrow is
an important day.

646
01:00:27.624 --> 01:00:29.626
The Aviator needs you.

647
01:00:32.170 --> 01:00:33.880
I let find you.

648
01:01:35.609 --> 01:01:36.735
Wow!

649
01:02:02.886 --> 01:02:04.888
Do you know how
to fly a plane?

650
01:02:08.183 --> 01:02:10.519
Yeah! I did not think so.

651
01:02:11.603 --> 01:02:13.355
Okay! Well...

652
01:02:18.443 --> 01:02:21.446
Yes! Yeah! I can do this.

653
01:02:22.155 --> 01:02:23.532
Here. Hold these.

654
01:03:43.653 --> 01:03:46.072
I think I have got
the hang of it now.

655
01:04:09.971 --> 01:04:11.431
I got you!

656
01:04:24.569 --> 01:04:26.321
Where are the stars?

657
01:04:31.034 --> 01:04:32.327
What is that?

658
01:04:35.830 --> 01:04:37.082
A star!

659
01:04:38.542 --> 01:04:41.169
Wait a minute.
That is not a star.

660
01:05:08.280 --> 01:05:11.116
The Aviator never
mentioned this place.

661
01:05:17.664 --> 01:05:18.748
Could it be?

662
01:05:21.501 --> 01:05:22.961
It is he! It is he!

663
01:05:23.336 --> 01:05:25.171
What is he doing here?

664
01:05:26.715 --> 01:05:28.091
Buckle up.

665
01:05:43.106 --> 01:05:44.357
We need a gap.

666
01:05:48.028 --> 01:05:49.988
I think see one up ahead.

667
01:05:56.828 --> 01:05:58.663
Prepare for landing.

668
01:06:04.169 --> 01:06:05.545
We did it!

669
01:06:12.169 --> 01:06:13.545
Oops!

670
01:06:28.943 --> 01:06:30.654
That was not too bad.

671
01:06:31.112 --> 01:06:32.989
Look! Up there.

672
01:06:46.586 --> 01:06:48.588
<i>Stand out of the vehicle.</i>

673
01:06:49.923 --> 01:06:52.300
<i>I said: Step out
of the vehicle.</I>

674
01:06:52.676 --> 01:06:54.969
I am very sorry. Officer.
If I could just explain...

675
01:06:55.053 --> 01:06:57.555
keep your hands where
I can see them.

676
01:07:04.187 --> 01:07:07.190
Unsafe speeding.
Unsafe lane changes.

677
01:07:07.273 --> 01:07:09.401
- Unsafe everything.
- What?

678
01:07:09.484 --> 01:07:10.735
Running multiple red lights.

679
01:07:10.902 --> 01:07:13.502
- Please! I am trying to find my friend.
- Destruction of city property.

680
01:07:13.530 --> 01:07:16.157
A friend of a friend.
We never officially met.

681
01:07:16.408 --> 01:07:19.369
No use of turn signals.
No signals at all.

682
01:07:19.494 --> 01:07:21.287
I just wanted to grab him
and, take him home.

683
01:07:21.871 --> 01:07:25.542
Attempted kidnapping!
Add that to the list.

684
01:07:25.625 --> 01:07:27.752
Attempted kidnapping.

685
01:07:29.754 --> 01:07:32.006
Hey! Are you...?

686
01:07:34.342 --> 01:07:36.761
Thank you.

687
01:07:36.845 --> 01:07:37.971
A Conceited Man.

688
01:07:39.431 --> 01:07:43.476
Insubordination to a uniformed
officer of the law. No less.

689
01:07:43.643 --> 01:07:45.019
I.

690
01:07:45.353 --> 01:07:46.521
Wait.

691
01:07:46.730 --> 01:07:48.398
Why are you not
on your planet?

692
01:07:52.694 --> 01:07:55.572
- Why are you so small?
- Because I am a child.

693
01:07:58.324 --> 01:08:00.952
That is absolutely
not allowed here.

694
01:08:01.244 --> 01:08:04.622
- Let us go!
- Hey! Hey! Hey!

695
01:08:06.666 --> 01:08:07.876
Not so fast!

696
01:08:15.258 --> 01:08:17.177
Thank you. Thank you.

697
01:08:17.802 --> 01:08:19.846
That is right. Go on.

698
01:08:29.814 --> 01:08:31.608
We can a need a disguise.

699
01:08:52.337 --> 01:08:54.923
Excuse me. I mean...

700
01:08:55.006 --> 01:08:57.425
Sorry! Sorry!

701
01:08:59.260 --> 01:09:01.137
Here are my subjects.

702
01:09:01.221 --> 01:09:02.514
Approach.

703
01:09:02.639 --> 01:09:04.015
Is that the king?

704
01:09:05.308 --> 01:09:06.768
- 67 Th floor.
- As you wish.

705
01:09:06.976 --> 01:09:08.311
- 27 Th floor.
- Granted.

706
01:09:08.394 --> 01:09:09.896
- 14 Th floor.
- Certainly.

707
01:09:09.979 --> 01:09:11.606
- 14 Th floor.
- Of course!

708
01:09:11.689 --> 01:09:13.149
- 34 Th floor.
- Happily.

709
01:09:15.360 --> 01:09:16.861
No.

710
01:09:19.239 --> 01:09:21.533
Top floor, please.

711
01:09:23.368 --> 01:09:25.245
What? Top floor?

712
01:09:26.371 --> 01:09:29.123
When conditions
are favorable?

713
01:09:29.290 --> 01:09:30.500
Your Majesty.

714
01:09:32.877 --> 01:09:34.212
Well...

715
01:09:35.505 --> 01:09:38.550
Conditions are favorable.

716
01:09:41.302 --> 01:09:42.720
It done.

717
01:10:05.910 --> 01:10:06.910
There he is!

718
01:10:13.877 --> 01:10:15.879
Little Prince! Little Prince!

719
01:10:16.462 --> 01:10:17.505
What?

720
01:10:20.884 --> 01:10:22.468
- I am so sorry.
- I am okay.

721
01:10:24.220 --> 01:10:25.263
My shift.

722
01:10:25.638 --> 01:10:27.765
- Are you okay?
- Yes. Yes.

723
01:10:27.932 --> 01:10:31.686
No! I was just... I was just taking
a little break. That is all.

724
01:10:32.145 --> 01:10:33.730
I thought you were
someone else.

725
01:10:33.897 --> 01:10:34.939
You did.

726
01:10:35.899 --> 01:10:38.151
That is great! That is great.

727
01:10:38.902 --> 01:10:40.194
Please do not report me.

728
01:10:40.278 --> 01:10:42.697
Breaks over. See?
I am working.

729
01:10:44.115 --> 01:10:45.700
Work. Work. Work.

730
01:10:45.992 --> 01:10:48.036
Do not need to report me.

731
01:10:48.369 --> 01:10:50.204
It was not him.

732
01:10:50.288 --> 01:10:51.998
What we gone do?

733
01:10:54.918 --> 01:10:56.336
Mr. Prince?

734
01:10:59.714 --> 01:11:01.132
Can it be?

735
01:11:01.799 --> 01:11:02.884
Excuse me?

736
01:11:07.221 --> 01:11:08.681
Oh! Man!

737
01:11:11.643 --> 01:11:13.144
I think you dropped this.

738
01:11:14.020 --> 01:11:15.188
My badge!

739
01:11:15.939 --> 01:11:18.775
- Catastrophe.
- It is he.

740
01:11:19.317 --> 01:11:21.694
- Can Me...
- What happened to you?

741
01:11:21.778 --> 01:11:23.446
Give me that.

742
01:11:23.571 --> 01:11:25.490
The Aviator is not
going to like this.

743
01:11:25.907 --> 01:11:28.701
- You are not supposed to be like this.
- Give it!

744
01:11:28.785 --> 01:11:30.620
Come on! Give me that!

745
01:11:30.954 --> 01:11:32.372
Thank you!

746
01:11:33.873 --> 01:11:36.167
How does this work?
Work is gone.

747
01:11:37.001 --> 01:11:39.253
I am working. See?
I am being essential.

748
01:11:39.337 --> 01:11:41.756
- Wait! Stop!
- No! No! Do not touch me.

749
01:11:41.839 --> 01:11:43.174
I know who you are!

750
01:11:43.257 --> 01:11:45.385
You are the Little Prince.
And, you are afraid of Baobabs!

751
01:11:45.468 --> 01:11:48.262
I am not... I am Mr. Prince,
the maintenance man.

752
01:11:48.346 --> 01:11:49.973
I am afraid of
the Businessman.

753
01:11:50.056 --> 01:11:52.475
An Aviator in the desert.
He drew you a sheep!

754
01:11:52.558 --> 01:11:53.977
You ask too many questions!

755
01:11:54.268 --> 01:11:56.104
You travel with a flock
of migrating birds.

756
01:11:56.187 --> 01:11:58.773
Go away. Excuse me!
I am very busy.

757
01:11:59.691 --> 01:12:02.276
You tamed a Fox.
A Fox like him!

758
01:12:02.360 --> 01:12:03.486
I never had a pet.

759
01:12:03.569 --> 01:12:06.531
He was not your pet.
He was your friend.

760
01:12:07.240 --> 01:12:09.701
Does it look like
I have time for friends.

761
01:12:09.826 --> 01:12:10.910
I am working!

762
01:12:12.996 --> 01:12:14.080
No!

763
01:12:15.665 --> 01:12:17.250
That was my last brush!

764
01:12:18.793 --> 01:12:20.461
I am going to be fire.

765
01:12:20.878 --> 01:12:22.463
Suppose to be my last chance.

766
01:12:22.880 --> 01:12:26.384
This is so unfair!
I was just doing my job.

767
01:12:26.884 --> 01:12:29.554
- Actually, there is one more.
- Thank you.

768
01:12:29.846 --> 01:12:31.889
- Now, I have to get back to work.
- Wait!

769
01:12:31.973 --> 01:12:34.434
You know! You are slowing
down my productivity!

770
01:12:34.600 --> 01:12:36.894
You had a Rose!

771
01:12:37.729 --> 01:12:38.771
What?

772
01:12:39.063 --> 01:12:40.148
A Rose.

773
01:12:40.565 --> 01:12:43.443
A beautiful one.
Miraculous even.

774
01:12:43.776 --> 01:12:45.820
One that was unique in
the entire world.

775
01:12:47.113 --> 01:12:49.699
You know! I have heard quite
enough of this nonsense.

776
01:12:49.866 --> 01:12:51.492
I have to work. Thank you.

777
01:12:51.576 --> 01:12:53.995
You have forgotten everything!

778
01:12:54.078 --> 01:12:56.330
I am very busy. No matter
the consequences.

779
01:12:56.414 --> 01:12:58.957
You have become just
another grown-up!

780
01:12:59.100 --> 01:13:00.375
Give me that.

781
01:13:03.296 --> 01:13:04.380
No!

782
01:13:09.896 --> 01:13:10.896
Oops!

783
01:13:10.928 --> 01:13:12.764
Why did you do that?

784
01:13:13.139 --> 01:13:14.849
Why did you do that...?

785
01:13:16.392 --> 01:13:18.644
It is all right. I
do not need crying.

786
01:13:19.062 --> 01:13:21.939
I do not need crying. I am
grown-up. I am a grown man.

787
01:13:24.484 --> 01:13:27.653
My brushes were knocking over.
I do not need crying.

788
01:13:28.946 --> 01:13:36.946
Crying... I... I... I...

789
01:13:39.457 --> 01:13:40.666
Well!

790
01:13:45.421 --> 01:13:47.632
Wait a minute.
Why are you so short?

791
01:13:48.591 --> 01:13:50.468
- Are you old?
- What?

792
01:13:50.843 --> 01:13:53.137
No! I am a child.

793
01:13:53.346 --> 01:13:55.223
Just like, you are
supposed to be.

794
01:13:55.306 --> 01:13:56.808
You are a child.

795
01:13:57.558 --> 01:14:00.478
Children are certainly
very, very, very, very odd.

796
01:14:01.604 --> 01:14:02.688
This is not good.

797
01:14:03.689 --> 01:14:05.525
I think I know someone
who can help.

798
01:14:09.278 --> 01:14:11.197
Are you sure about this?

799
01:14:20.998 --> 01:14:22.583
Mr. Prince.

800
01:14:23.000 --> 01:14:25.294
What a pleasant surprise.

801
01:14:28.756 --> 01:14:30.800
This child needs your help.

802
01:14:30.883 --> 01:14:32.593
Does she?

803
01:14:34.053 --> 01:14:38.266
Here. We do not normally
allow little dogs.

804
01:14:38.766 --> 01:14:42.186
But, for you. We will make
an exception. Will we?

805
01:14:44.438 --> 01:14:45.648
Delightful!

806
01:14:45.731 --> 01:14:48.234
Come in. Come here!

807
01:14:50.194 --> 01:14:53.114
So how have you been?
Things good?

808
01:14:53.406 --> 01:14:55.199
I love my job
cleaning the roof.

809
01:14:55.283 --> 01:14:57.493
Wonderful. Yes!

810
01:15:06.627 --> 01:15:09.964
- Anything inessential.
- Must make essential.

811
01:15:10.047 --> 01:15:12.008
Well done. Mr. Prince.

812
01:15:15.386 --> 01:15:20.433
You see. It is a magnificent thing
the Businessman has created here.

813
01:15:20.516 --> 01:15:23.436
You might even call
it a work of art.

814
01:15:24.145 --> 01:15:26.355
But, of course!
You would be wrong.

815
01:15:26.439 --> 01:15:28.941
Very, very wrong.

816
01:15:29.442 --> 01:15:31.152
Nothing as trivial as that.

817
01:15:31.235 --> 01:15:32.320
The plane!

818
01:15:32.403 --> 01:15:36.449
It is much more important.
Much more essential.

819
01:15:38.242 --> 01:15:39.744
No! Wait!

820
01:15:39.827 --> 01:15:41.746
How could you?
You said: You would help.

821
01:15:41.829 --> 01:15:42.597
GRADUATES

822
01:15:42.780 --> 01:15:44.924
I am. That is how
they helped me!

823
01:15:46.918 --> 01:15:48.711
Mr. Prince!

824
01:15:48.794 --> 01:15:51.797
It seems that you have
finally done something.

825
01:15:54.425 --> 01:15:55.968
Let us right.

826
01:15:57.720 --> 01:16:00.514
You will tell the Businessman.
How essential I have been?

827
01:16:00.723 --> 01:16:03.309
Yes. I must certainly will.

828
01:16:05.394 --> 01:16:07.396
The Businessman told me.

829
01:16:07.480 --> 01:16:10.858
This evidence of childhood
you brought with you.

830
01:16:10.942 --> 01:16:13.527
- Please! Those are important!
- No!

831
01:16:13.611 --> 01:16:15.613
There is nothing essential
in here at all.

832
01:16:19.075 --> 01:16:20.451
It is time...

833
01:16:21.535 --> 01:16:22.578
To grow up.

834
01:16:22.787 --> 01:16:26.332
THE ESSENTIAL GUIDE TO
EVERYTHING ESSENTIAL

835
01:16:27.458 --> 01:16:30.294
How could everything essential
fit into just one book?

836
01:16:30.503 --> 01:16:32.546
It is incredibly succinct.

837
01:16:33.214 --> 01:16:34.465
And, single-spaced.

838
01:16:34.614 --> 01:16:35.665
So what?

839
01:16:35.874 --> 01:16:39.553
I am supposed to read this over
and, repeatedly, until I am old?

840
01:16:39.845 --> 01:16:40.845
Not at all.

841
01:16:41.472 --> 01:16:46.060
Here, we take a more accelerated
approach to growing up.

842
01:16:48.980 --> 01:16:51.315
Is does not that
right? Mr. Prince!

843
01:16:51.482 --> 01:16:53.317
No, never mind.

844
01:16:53.401 --> 01:16:56.821
Those blink eyes. You have
forgotten everything can do.

845
01:17:03.661 --> 01:17:07.498
Now! You are going to a
slight pinch. Just relax.

846
01:17:08.082 --> 01:17:09.750
Yes! Please sign there.

847
01:17:09.917 --> 01:17:12.378
A consent form releasing me.
The Businessman.

848
01:17:12.461 --> 01:17:14.714
- And the corporation from all liability.
- Help!

849
01:17:14.797 --> 01:17:16.257
In case of accidental death.

850
01:17:16.340 --> 01:17:19.093
Or dismemberment during
the centralizing process. Right!

851
01:17:19.510 --> 01:17:21.304
I am trying to help you!

852
01:17:21.387 --> 01:17:24.056
I am going to make
a wonderful grown-up.

853
01:17:26.350 --> 01:17:27.393
Leave them!

854
01:17:30.229 --> 01:17:32.356
I said: Leave them!

855
01:17:32.940 --> 01:17:35.693
Act of your age, Mr. Prince!

856
01:17:36.193 --> 01:17:38.195
Remember. You are
a graduate of my class.

857
01:17:40.489 --> 01:17:42.867
Stop! What do you think
are doing?

858
01:17:48.914 --> 01:17:51.167
Return to your desk. Please.

859
01:17:57.514 --> 01:17:59.167
Wow!

860
01:17:59.717 --> 01:18:01.719
I did not think that through.

861
01:18:02.345 --> 01:18:05.222
The Businessman is going
to be very disappoint in me.

862
01:18:05.639 --> 01:18:08.267
Thank you. Why?

863
01:18:09.143 --> 01:18:12.104
I never knew what this was.
Or, where I even got it.

864
01:18:12.188 --> 01:18:14.565
But, I thought maybe
it was important.

865
01:18:15.399 --> 01:18:16.442
Your sheep!

866
01:18:16.525 --> 01:18:17.902
My sheep?

867
01:18:19.362 --> 01:18:20.363
I do not get it.

868
01:18:20.696 --> 01:18:22.406
The Aviator gave it to you.

869
01:18:22.490 --> 01:18:24.909
In the desert on Earth.
To eat the Baobabs.

870
01:18:25.409 --> 01:18:27.411
- Catastrophe.
- Catastrophe.

871
01:18:27.745 --> 01:18:28.788
That is right.

872
01:18:29.080 --> 01:18:31.207
The Aviator drew all
of these for you.

873
01:18:31.624 --> 01:18:35.669
- He really needs you right now.
- Me? He needs me.

874
01:18:39.006 --> 01:18:42.927
<i>Growing up is not the problem.
Forgetting is.</i>

875
01:18:47.098 --> 01:18:48.265
I have an idea.

876
01:18:49.016 --> 01:18:51.310
We just get a need... The plane!

877
01:18:54.688 --> 01:18:55.731
There it is!

878
01:18:56.565 --> 01:18:57.942
It is okay.

879
01:19:05.157 --> 01:19:06.325
Hurry!

880
01:19:32.601 --> 01:19:34.437
We did it!

881
01:19:39.567 --> 01:19:40.901
No!

882
01:19:46.323 --> 01:19:47.575
Which button?

883
01:19:53.747 --> 01:19:54.915
No!

884
01:20:22.026 --> 01:20:23.068
Yes!

885
01:20:24.653 --> 01:20:27.239
We can catch it on top
of the next pile!

886
01:20:27.615 --> 01:20:29.575
Wait! Where is Mr. Prince?

887
01:20:41.045 --> 01:20:42.338
I remember these.

888
01:20:43.339 --> 01:20:45.132
Stars.

889
01:20:45.216 --> 01:20:46.800
Put are they all doing here?

890
01:20:53.516 --> 01:20:55.310
The stars appeared.
The stars appeared.

891
01:20:55.893 --> 01:20:58.229
The stars are beautiful.

892
01:20:58.312 --> 01:21:01.106
Because of a flower
that cannot be seeing.

893
01:21:02.733 --> 01:21:05.611
Because of a flower
that cannot be seeing.

894
01:21:05.861 --> 01:21:07.029
Your Rose!

895
01:21:07.404 --> 01:21:09.907
I have a Rose.

896
01:21:10.824 --> 01:21:13.410
I see you have found
my collection.

897
01:21:13.494 --> 01:21:18.707
501.622,731 stars.

898
01:21:19.583 --> 01:21:21.877
You? You did this.

899
01:21:21.961 --> 01:21:24.046
Wait! You are suppose
to just count the stars.

900
01:21:24.296 --> 01:21:28.926
Own! Say it with me.
Own! I own the stars.

901
01:21:31.387 --> 01:21:33.264
Thank you. Thank you.

902
01:21:34.765 --> 01:21:38.352
They used to be merely
little golden objects in the sky.

903
01:21:38.435 --> 01:21:41.939
That set lazy men to idle
dreaming.

904
01:21:42.356 --> 01:21:46.860
But now, the stars have
finally be made essential.

905
01:21:47.945 --> 01:21:49.238
Hey! Where did you get that?

906
01:21:50.698 --> 01:21:52.116
She is curious.

907
01:21:52.199 --> 01:21:54.201
Is not that just like a child?

908
01:21:57.454 --> 01:21:58.497
No!

909
01:21:58.581 --> 01:21:59.623
Thank you.

910
01:21:59.707 --> 01:22:01.083
All right! All right! Enough.

911
01:22:01.166 --> 01:22:03.335
- Thank you.
- All right!

912
01:22:04.253 --> 01:22:05.504
Enough!

913
01:22:07.923 --> 01:22:10.718
What are you going to do
with all the stars?

914
01:22:10.801 --> 01:22:13.387
Do not worry, my little girl.

915
01:22:13.470 --> 01:22:15.806
I put the stars to good use.

916
01:22:34.199 --> 01:22:38.829
There. You see. The inessential
has become perfectly essential.

917
01:22:39.496 --> 01:22:41.874
How it should be for all things.

918
01:22:42.374 --> 01:22:43.751
Take her back to the classroom.

919
01:22:43.834 --> 01:22:45.586
Make sure no one interferes.

920
01:22:46.337 --> 01:22:49.089
- No! Stop! Put me down. I cannot.
- Stop!

921
01:22:49.340 --> 01:22:52.092
- Do not let them do this to me.
- You not allowed.

922
01:22:52.801 --> 01:22:54.386
- Wait!
- Wait?

923
01:22:55.137 --> 01:22:57.848
I have given you 371 jobs.

924
01:22:57.931 --> 01:23:00.976
And you have be fired
from 370 of them.

925
01:23:01.060 --> 01:23:04.772
I think it is time you get back
to work. My little failure.

926
01:23:05.731 --> 01:23:09.109
- No! Please! He got leave!
- Stop wriggling.

927
01:23:10.444 --> 01:23:11.904
Stop!

928
01:23:12.321 --> 01:23:14.948
- Take your hands off her.
- What? Stop?

929
01:23:15.616 --> 01:23:18.243
I am not a failure.

930
01:23:18.661 --> 01:23:19.745
I am the Little Prince.

931
01:23:20.037 --> 01:23:21.037
What?

932
01:23:22.373 --> 01:23:26.210
He thinks he is little.
And, a Prince!

933
01:23:30.130 --> 01:23:31.507
Wonderful.

934
01:23:31.674 --> 01:23:34.093
Look at me! I am a Bumblebee.

935
01:23:34.176 --> 01:23:36.720
What are you? A duck?

936
01:23:42.059 --> 01:23:43.310
He is hopeless.

937
01:23:44.895 --> 01:23:47.815
I am not hopeless.
I am hopeful!

938
01:23:48.565 --> 01:23:50.984
That is right!
I am full of hope!

939
01:23:51.902 --> 01:23:53.404
And, I love a Rose!

940
01:23:53.862 --> 01:23:55.864
She loves me.
And, she is waiting for me!

941
01:23:56.323 --> 01:23:57.741
So...

942
01:23:57.825 --> 01:23:59.660
I do not think I want to work
for you anymore.

943
01:24:00.244 --> 01:24:01.620
And, of...

944
01:24:02.746 --> 01:24:03.831
I quit!

945
01:24:07.876 --> 01:24:09.670
I quit!

946
01:24:17.219 --> 01:24:18.219
That pile!

947
01:24:22.725 --> 01:24:26.186
When are you going to forget
about being a child?

948
01:24:26.854 --> 01:24:27.896
Never!

949
01:24:28.854 --> 01:24:29.896
Ouch!

950
01:24:30.691 --> 01:24:31.817
Sorry, Mr. Prince!

951
01:24:32.276 --> 01:24:35.654
No. It is my fault. My face
should not have been there.

952
01:24:35.904 --> 01:24:36.947
Good.

953
01:24:45.164 --> 01:24:46.290
No.

954
01:24:51.003 --> 01:24:52.296
I am scared.

955
01:25:05.203 --> 01:25:07.296
Get in there!

956
01:25:08.896 --> 01:25:10.314
Hang on!

957
01:25:21.158 --> 01:25:23.327
- I will right back!
- Where are you going?

958
01:25:23.561 --> 01:25:24.561
What are you doing?

959
01:25:26.997 --> 01:25:28.415
That is not good.

960
01:25:32.197 --> 01:25:33.415
Wait!

961
01:25:36.799 --> 01:25:40.177
I will grow up, but I will never
be a fool like you!

962
01:25:53.357 --> 01:25:54.441
Wow!

963
01:26:11.792 --> 01:26:12.835
No!

964
01:26:20.175 --> 01:26:21.301
I got you!

965
01:26:23.175 --> 01:26:24.175
You all right?

966
01:26:31.520 --> 01:26:32.563
I got you, too.

967
01:27:01.758 --> 01:27:03.093
Wonderful!

968
01:27:13.646 --> 01:27:18.233
This is very, very, very
bad for business.

969
01:27:20.570 --> 01:27:23.071
That was amazing!

970
01:27:26.867 --> 01:27:28.243
The stars are back.

971
01:27:30.037 --> 01:27:32.331
I forgot how beautiful they are.

972
01:27:34.082 --> 01:27:38.003
- Look! Asteroid 325!
- You are remembering!

973
01:27:38.086 --> 01:27:39.671
And, 326!

974
01:27:41.048 --> 01:27:42.716
And, 327!

975
01:27:43.258 --> 01:27:44.343
And, 328!

976
01:27:44.426 --> 01:27:46.011
It is working! It is working!

977
01:27:47.638 --> 01:27:49.973
Look! B-612!

978
01:27:52.392 --> 01:27:53.477
The Baobabs.

979
01:27:59.274 --> 01:28:01.276
Your Rose! She is there!

980
01:28:02.235 --> 01:28:03.570
Hold on!

981
01:28:04.029 --> 01:28:05.906
You are not gone try landing.
Are you?

982
01:28:07.699 --> 01:28:10.911
No. No. Stop! Stop!
Turn around! Stop!

983
01:28:11.699 --> 01:28:12.911
God!

984
01:28:19.252 --> 01:28:20.504
What is happening?

985
01:28:21.046 --> 01:28:23.423
We are falling.

986
01:28:26.259 --> 01:28:28.261
- Where are we going now?
- Just still.

987
01:28:30.259 --> 01:28:31.261
Come on! Jesus!

988
01:28:38.259 --> 01:28:39.261
Wow!

989
01:28:51.952 --> 01:28:53.036
Let us go.

990
01:29:14.474 --> 01:29:16.309
Over here! Over here!
I found her!

991
01:29:22.190 --> 01:29:23.275
Look.

992
01:29:24.609 --> 01:29:25.861
My Rose.

993
01:29:34.786 --> 01:29:36.121
It is she.

994
01:29:52.186 --> 01:29:53.621
No!

995
01:30:05.650 --> 01:30:06.693
No!

996
01:30:15.744 --> 01:30:17.162
No! How can this be?

997
01:30:21.833 --> 01:30:24.044
I am so sorry.

998
01:30:26.254 --> 01:30:28.006
You are supposed to be
with her.

999
01:30:32.511 --> 01:30:34.679
I am going to lose him, too.

1000
01:30:37.557 --> 01:30:39.017
And, grow up.

1001
01:30:40.602 --> 01:30:42.104
And, forget all about him.

1002
01:30:44.606 --> 01:30:46.274
Forget all.

1003
01:30:46.691 --> 01:30:48.026
Forever.

1004
01:30:50.445 --> 01:30:52.531
I do not want to lose him.

1005
01:30:54.449 --> 01:30:55.534
Do not cry.

1006
01:30:59.579 --> 01:31:01.706
How can I not be crying?

1007
01:31:32.821 --> 01:31:34.239
I can see her.

1008
01:31:41.413 --> 01:31:43.748
She was not a common Rose.

1009
01:31:44.749 --> 01:31:48.128
She was the only one of her kind
in the whole universe.

1010
01:31:50.755 --> 01:31:52.340
I remember her.

1011
01:31:52.757 --> 01:31:54.426
I remember all of it.

1012
01:31:54.926 --> 01:31:56.136
She is not gone.

1013
01:31:57.095 --> 01:31:58.263
She is still here.

1014
01:31:58.513 --> 01:32:03.056
It is only with the heart
that one can see rightly.

1015
01:32:07.981 --> 01:32:09.649
He will always be with me.

1016
01:32:11.276 --> 01:32:12.986
I understand now.

1017
01:32:26.291 --> 01:32:29.461
- Please. Tell the Aviator I remember him!
- I will!

1018
01:32:30.337 --> 01:32:31.546
Do not forget.

1019
01:32:31.880 --> 01:32:33.048
I will not!

1020
01:32:33.131 --> 01:32:35.800
I will not forget any of it!
I promise.

1021
01:33:12.337 --> 01:33:13.463
Sweetie?

1022
01:33:13.546 --> 01:33:14.589
Yes?

1023
01:33:15.340 --> 01:33:17.509
- We are late.
- What?

1024
01:33:18.009 --> 01:33:19.052
No. We are not.

1025
01:33:19.177 --> 01:33:21.513
We need to stop by the hospital
before of school.

1026
01:33:26.726 --> 01:33:31.231
122. 123. 124...

1027
01:33:33.566 --> 01:33:35.110
Okay.

1028
01:34:38.798 --> 01:34:40.091
You are here.

1029
01:34:42.969 --> 01:34:44.012
I am sorry.

1030
01:34:45.263 --> 01:34:47.932
I am so sorry
for what I said.

1031
01:34:50.101 --> 01:34:52.312
I do not even remember.

1032
01:34:53.772 --> 01:34:54.856
That is sweet.

1033
01:34:54.939 --> 01:34:58.610
No. I do not even remember
who you are.

1034
01:35:00.820 --> 01:35:03.615
I got you. Did not I?

1035
01:35:07.869 --> 01:35:10.121
I have something to show you.

1036
01:35:22.169 --> 01:35:24.921
LE PETIT PRINCE

1037
01:35:25.637 --> 01:35:27.013
You did this.

1038
01:35:33.853 --> 01:35:36.689
All my drawings. All in order!

1039
01:35:41.069 --> 01:35:43.530
This is so wonderful.

1040
01:35:49.411 --> 01:35:50.829
Sweetheart!

1041
01:35:53.331 --> 01:35:57.836
" You run the risk of weeping a little,
if you let yourself get tamed."

1042
01:36:04.259 --> 01:36:07.429
You are gone a make
a wonderful grown-up.

1043
01:36:16.688 --> 01:36:18.189
Thank you.

1044
01:36:20.024 --> 01:36:21.526
Did you see this?

1045
01:36:28.950 --> 01:36:30.535
It is wonderful.

1046
01:36:30.702 --> 01:36:33.037
Look. You see.
That is the Fox.

1047
01:36:33.872 --> 01:36:35.290
My Fox.

1048
01:38:54.512 --> 01:38:57.765
You probably think
this is a hat, but it is not.

1049
01:39:15.428 --> 01:39:19.748
THE LITTLE PRINCE
Translation and review by Angel.
